# MF Overhaul 0.4.8: test 0.4.7 proved c13 slot 3 is the size-growth fraction (puffs stayed tiny at 1.2) and that the burst smoke
#   rises on its own whatever the launch spread, speed factor or pull-down: the BROB burst generator sends its puffs up, and vanilla
#   hides that by letting them die in 12-15 s. So the engine-realistic structure is: a dark smoke burst that lives like vanilla
#   (12/14/16 s, fade from 0.4) while the long persistence is carried by the dust skirt, which stays low (26/34/40 s from 0.3.57).
#   Launch deltas 06/07 retired (vanilla launch again). Smoke: growth 0.15/0.2 restored, puffs 24/30/40, 1/1.5/2 -> 10/15/20 m,
#   two tints, alpha 0xC0, animation 5, pull-down -0.1 (vanilla).
